[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: An injected script's leading comment swallows its shebang

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[WORK]
UID: WORK-INJECTED-COMMENT-SHEBANG
TITLE: An injected script's leading comment swallows its shebang
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
In the bash-in-nix injection extractor, an injected item whose body opens with
a leading comment swallows the shebang line into that comment, so the first
line of the script is reported as part of the comment block rather than as the
interpreter line. Line ranges for such an item start one line late. Cheapest
fix: treat a first-line shebang as its own node before the comment grouping
runs.
<<<
